# H2.12 / S2-23 — Trivy suppressions for the built images.
#
# Deliberately EMPTY. Unlike the npm and pip baselines, image scanning starts
# clean: the images are rebuilt from a pinned base on every run, so a HIGH or
# CRITICAL here is something a base-image bump or a package pin can fix, not
# historical debt to be ratcheted down.
#
# `ignore-unfixed: true` is already set in the workflow, so findings with no
# published fix do not reach this file — anything that lands here is fixable
# and should be fixed rather than listed.
#
# To suppress one, add its CVE id on its own line WITH a comment giving the
# reason and the date. An entry with no reason is indistinguishable from an
# entry nobody understood.
